CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ range \| closure: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ other specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ closure \| closure: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
function_template_identifier rendered the requires-clause without its
`type' sub-nodes, where the substituted enclosing argument lives; tag types
there are now rendered.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
